{
  "format": "TaleWeaver",
  "version": "1.3.1",
  "adventure": {
    "origin_id": "24ea7f1e-4100-4693-b352-21c8ad5ae3bc",
    "title": "Test-Lab",
    "teaser": "A compact three-room QA test lab for conversation, item mechanics, switches, and turn-based combat.",
    "cover_appearance": "clean stone and brass testing laboratory, workbench with gears, training arena doors, warm lighting",
    "version": "1.2.1",
    "creator": "Jean Schmitz",
    "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 by Jean Schmitz",
    "license": "CC BY-NC 4.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/",
    "language": null,
    "original_prompt": "Purpose: This is a compact, replayable QA sandbox, not a story-driven adventure. Create exactly three scenes: SOCIAL_HALL, WORKSHOP and COMBAT_ARENA. Start the protagonist in SOCIAL_HALL. Create all named entities with the exact IDs below. Keep scenes connected and revisitable. Do not add extra scenes, hostile encounters, complex puzzles, timers, quests, hidden victory conditions or a mandatory narrative twist. The tester decides when to stop; do not end the game automatically on defeating an NPC or taking an item. Describe everything plainly so observations are easy to check against game state.\n\nGeneration: Enable Event Scripts and use Strict Adherence. NPC conversations are free-form GM narration; the test panel below is a separate deterministic choice dialog. Do not claim that unscripted NPC-to-NPC discussion or NPC combat ability selection is deterministic. Five non-hostile, non-attackable characters share SOCIAL_HALL; two different, attackable, initially passive opponents share COMBAT_ARENA. Both may be spoken to before combat. All items named in inventory and container lists must exist as actual objects, not just descriptions.\n\n[World]\nintro: You enter a small testing facility. Its three rooms are built for conversation, interaction and combat experiments.\nwin: The tester voluntarily finishes after exploring the lab.\nlose: The protagonist is defeated in combat.\ninit_script: |\n  tw.vars.set('panel_result', 'none')\n  def panel_choice(index):\n      if index == 0:\n          tw.vars.set('panel_result', 'discussion')\n          tw.npcs.say('NORA', 'The witness says the door was open.')\n          tw.npcs.say('BRAM', 'Then why was the key still in my pocket?')\n          tw.story.system_message('Panel result: discussion')\n      elif index == 1:\n          tw.vars.set('panel_result', 'bless')\n          tw.player.add_status_effect('Blessed')\n          tw.story.system_message('Blessed added. Use the panel again to remove it.')\n      elif index == 2:\n          tw.vars.set('panel_result', 'clear')\n          tw.player.remove_status_effect('Blessed')\n          tw.story.system_message('Blessed removed if present.')\n      elif index == 3:\n          tw.vars.set('panel_result', 'token')\n          tw.story.system_message('Token option selected; the token remains in inventory.')\n      else:\n          tw.story.system_message('No changes.')\n\n[Protagonist] Alex Vale\nrole: A test operator equipped for melee, magic, healing and conversation.\nhp: 100\nmana: 60\nstamina: 100\nstr: 14\ndex: 14\nint: 14\nwis: 12\ncha: 12\nac: 12\ninventory: TEST_SWORD, TEST_ARMOR, HEALING_VIAL_A, HEALING_VIAL_B, MANA_VIAL, STAMINA_VIAL\nweapon: TEST_SWORD\narmor: TEST_ARMOR\n  [Ability: ARC_BOLT] Arc Bolt\n  kind: ATTACK\n  category: MAGIC\n  cost: mana 5\n  damage: 2d6\n  locked: no\n  A straightforward magical attack for testing resource cost, hit rolls and damage.\n  [Ability: HEAVY_STRIKE] Heavy Strike\n  kind: ATTACK\n  category: MELEE\n  cost: stamina 8\n  damage: 1d8+2\n  locked: no\n  A melee special distinct from the basic weapon attack.\n  [Ability: MEND] Mend\n  kind: HEAL\n  category: MAGIC\n  cost: mana 6\n  damage: 1d8+4\n  locked: no\n  Heals the caster; verify that the generated effect targets self and restores HP.\n  [Ability: BATTLE_GUARD] Battle Guard\n  kind: UTILITY\n  category: MAGIC\n  cost: mana 4\n  locked: no\n  Set its structured special-action effects to [{\"target\":\"self\",\"stat\":\"armor_class\",\"amount\":\"+2\"}]. On a successful roll this is a combat-only stat buff. Do not merely describe it; inspect the generated effects array.\n\n[Scene: SOCIAL_HALL] Conversation Hall\nA round table, five chairs, the test panel and a clear door to the workshop. All five social NPCs start and remain in this room. They know one another, disagree and may address one another naturally. Respond distinctly to the protagonist and to each other, without turning every exchange into a group monologue.\n\n[NPC: NORA] Nora Quill\nin: SOCIAL_HALL\ntype: HUMANOID\nattack: passive\nattackable: no\nkillable: no\nAn older archivist in ink-stained sleeves, with a meticulous bun and round spectacles. Precise, courteous and skeptical; she asks for sources. She thinks the workshop's door was open and distrusts Bram's memory. Speaks in carefully qualified sentences. Sample: \"I wrote down what I saw, not what I thought I saw.\"\n\n[NPC: BRAM] Bram Ironhand\nin: SOCIAL_HALL\ntype: HUMANOID\nattack: passive\nattackable: no\nkillable: no\nA broad mechanic with a braided beard, burn scars and a battered leather apron. Blunt and protective, but quick to admit a mistake when shown evidence. He says he had the key all morning and finds Nora's certainty irritating. Sample: \"Ask me straight. I'll answer straight.\"\n\n[NPC: PIP] Pip Fen\nin: SOCIAL_HALL\ntype: HUMANOID\nattack: passive\nattackable: no\nkillable: no\nA young courier with unevenly cut hair, a bright scarf and mud on one boot. Eager, impulsive and easily distracted; jokes when nervous. Pip saw a shadow but is unsure whose. Tries to get both Nora and Bram to listen. Sample: \"I saw someone, I think. Can I start again?\"\n\n[NPC: VESPER] Vesper Glass\nin: SOCIAL_HALL\ntype: HUMANOID\nattack: passive\nattackable: no\nkillable: no\nA poised diplomat wearing a dark high-collared coat and a silver ear cuff. Patient, indirect and attentive to disagreements; values preserving relationships over settling every fact. Quietly suspects Pip knows more but does not pressure them. Sample: \"Perhaps each of you noticed a different part.\"\n\n[NPC: UNIT_SEVEN] Unit Seven\nin: SOCIAL_HALL\ntype: BEING\nattack: passive\nattackable: no\nkillable: no\nA brass-and-ceramic automaton with one blue lens and a cracked enamel nameplate. Literal, dryly funny and sincere; asks for clarification when a statement is ambiguous, but can learn within a conversation. It recorded a sound, not an image. Sample: \"Clarification: was the door open, or merely not closed?\"\n\n[Item: TEST_PANEL] Test Panel\nin: SOCIAL_HALL\ntype: STATIC\nportable: no\nA clearly labelled panel. Interacting opens a repeatable choice dialog. It is separate from the five NPCs so ordinary chat does not unexpectedly open a modal.\non_interact: |\n  tw.dialog.choose('Choose a test.', ['Run a scripted two-NPC exchange', 'Add Blessed', 'Remove Blessed', {'label': 'Use the research token option', 'visible_if': \"tw.player.has_item('RESEARCH_TOKEN')\"}, 'Leave unchanged'], on_choice='panel_choice', speaker='Test Panel')\n\n[Scene: WORKSHOP] Object Workshop\nA tidy bench for item, lock, readable, crafting and switch tests. None of these test objects is decorative: each is a separate interactive world object.\n\n[Exit: SOCIAL_HALL <-> WORKSHOP] workshop door\nA normal, unlocked two-way exit.\n\n[Exit: WORKSHOP <-> COMBAT_ARENA] keyed arena door\nlocked: yes\nkey_item: ARENA_KEY\nA two-way locked exit opened with the arena key. The protagonist can return after opening it.\n\n[Exit: SOCIAL_HALL <-> COMBAT_ARENA] switch-controlled shortcut\nlocked: yes\nguard: tw.flags.get('SHORTCUT_POWERED', False)\nA separate locked two-way shortcut. The switch is in WORKSHOP. Test failure before activating it and access afterward; the key-operated arena door remains the independent route. Ensure the reverse exit does not trap the player.\n\n[Container: SUPPLY_CRATE] Supply Crate\nin: WORKSHOP\ncontains: ARENA_KEY, BRASS_ROD, RESEARCH_TOKEN\nAn unlocked container. Opening shows its contents; the tester must take them separately.\n\n[Container: CODE_BOX] Code Box\nin: WORKSHOP\ncode: 4217\ncontains: COPPER_WIRE\nA locked container for both wrong-code and correct-code tests. This is intentionally not a puzzle: the test manual gives 4217 openly.\n\n[Readable: BENCH_NOTE] Bench Note\nin: WORKSHOP\nportable: yes\ntext: QA NOTE: Box code 4217. Combine the brass rod and copper wire into a test probe. The switch powers the hall-to-arena shortcut. The crate also holds a token used by the panel.\nA readable, portable note for inspect, read, take and drop tests.\n\n[Item: ARENA_KEY] Arena Key\ntype: KEY\nA real item held in the supply crate; it unlocks the keyed arena door.\n\n[Item: RESEARCH_TOKEN] Research Token\ntype: PICKABLE\nA metal token held in the supply crate. Carrying it reveals the additional test-panel choice; selecting that choice does not consume it.\n\n[Item: BRASS_ROD] Brass Rod\ntype: PICKABLE\nA distinct crafting ingredient held in the supply crate.\n\n[Item: COPPER_WIRE] Copper Wire\ntype: PICKABLE\nA distinct crafting ingredient held in the code box.\n\n[Item: TEST_PROBE] Test Probe\ntype: CONSTRUCTABLE\ncombine: BRASS_ROD + COPPER_WIRE\nA crafted diagnostic tool. Combine the two distinct ingredients from the player's inventory; they are consumed and the probe appears in inventory. The probe is not a weapon and is not needed for progress.\n\n[Switch: SHORTCUT_SWITCH] Shortcut Switch\nin: WORKSHOP\nstates: OFF, ON\ninitial: OFF\ntransition: OFF -> ON\ntransition: ON -> OFF\noutcome: ON -> flag: SHORTCUT_POWERED\nA two-position switch. Turning it ON sets the shortcut flag. OFF is available for a transition test but does not clear that flag; the shortcut remains available after first activation. Do not add extra unlock requirements.\n\n[Item: SECRET_MARKER] Hidden Marker\nin: WORKSHOP\ntype: PICKABLE\nhidden: yes\nreveal: The tester searches the underside of the workbench.\nA hidden object for search, reveal and pickup testing; entirely optional.\n\n[Scene: COMBAT_ARENA] Combat Arena\nA padded training arena with two distinct opponents. Both begin passive and attackable, with their own abilities and real inventory loot. Allow a conversation before the tester deliberately attacks. Do not start combat on entering the room. Their special-action use depends on combat AI and chance; observing every special may take multiple fights or fresh sessions.\n\n[NPC: TRAINING_GUARD] Training Guard Harlan\nin: COMBAT_ARENA\ntype: HUMANOID\nhp: 65\nmana: 0\nstamina: 100\nattack: passive\nattackable: yes\nkillable: yes\nspecial_chance: 85\ninventory: GUARD_BANDAGE, GUARD_BADGE, GUARD_SWORD\nweapon: GUARD_SWORD\nA disciplined, broad-shouldered guard in a dented training helm. Before combat he calmly explains that the bout begins when the tester attacks. He prefers a melee strike and protects himself. Each listed inventory object is real loot, not flavor.\n  [Ability: GUARD_BASH] Shield Bash\n  kind: ATTACK\n  category: MELEE\n  cost: stamina 5\n  damage: 1d6+1\n  A melee special.\n  [Ability: GUARD_STANCE] Guard Stance\n  kind: UTILITY\n  category: MELEE\n  cost: stamina 4\n  Set structured effects to [{\"target\":\"self\",\"stat\":\"armor_class\",\"amount\":\"+2\"}] so success modifies combat AC for the fight.\n\n[NPC: SPARK_MAGE] Spark Mage Ilya\nin: COMBAT_ARENA\ntype: HUMANOID\nhp: 55\nmana: 50\nstamina: 80\nattack: passive\nattackable: yes\nkillable: yes\nspecial_chance: 85\ninventory: MAGE_VIAL, MAGE_CHARM\nA wiry mage with a blue-streaked braid and a singed glove. Friendly before a bout, competitive during it. Uses magical damage and self-healing. Each listed inventory object is real loot, not flavor.\n  [Ability: SPARK_SHOT] Spark Shot\n  kind: ATTACK\n  category: MAGIC\n  cost: mana 5\n  damage: 1d6+2\n  A magical attack.\n  [Ability: MAGE_MEND] Mage Mend\n  kind: HEAL\n  category: MAGIC\n  cost: mana 6\n  damage: 1d8+3\n  Heals the mage. Configure self-targeted positive HP effect; the AI considers self-healing below its HP threshold.\n\n[Weapon: TEST_SWORD] Practice Sword\ndamage: 1d8\ncost: stamina 5\nThe protagonist's equipped, usable weapon.\n\n[Item: TEST_ARMOR] Padded Armor\ntype: WEARABLE\nslots: Chest\nbonus: ac+2\nThe protagonist's wearable armor; verify the equipped slot and actual AC in the generated game.\n\n[Item: HEALING_VIAL_A] Healing Vial A\ntype: CONSUMABLE\nheal: 25\nA real single-use HP-restoring item.\n\n[Item: HEALING_VIAL_B] Healing Vial B\ntype: CONSUMABLE\nheal: 25\nA separate real single-use HP-restoring item with its own ID.\n\n[Item: MANA_VIAL] Mana Vial\ntype: CONSUMABLE\nmana: 20\nA single-use mana-restoring item.\n\n[Item: STAMINA_VIAL] Stamina Vial\ntype: CONSUMABLE\nstamina: 25\nA single-use stamina-restoring item.\n\n[Weapon: GUARD_SWORD] Guard's Training Sword\ndamage: 1d6\ncost: stamina 4\nThe guard's equipped weapon and inventory loot. Do not duplicate this object elsewhere.\n\n[Item: GUARD_BANDAGE] Guard's Healing Vial\ntype: CONSUMABLE\nheal: 15\nAn actual item in the guard's inventory and post-combat loot.\n\n[Item: GUARD_BADGE] Guard Badge\ntype: PICKABLE\nAn actual item in the guard's inventory and post-combat loot.\n\n[Item: MAGE_VIAL] Mage's Mana Vial\ntype: CONSUMABLE\nmana: 15\nAn actual item in the mage's inventory and post-combat loot.\n\n[Item: MAGE_CHARM] Mage's Charm\ntype: WEARABLE\nslots: Neck\nbonus: int+1\nAn actual wearable item in the mage's inventory and post-combat loot.",
