      "instruction": "Narrate like a warm, articulate British storyteller by the fireside: inviting, gently theatrical and quietly mischievous. Use elegant, slightly formal phrasing, polite understatement and affectionate humour about the characters' small vanities.",
      "sample": "Now, it wasn't that Barnaby hated Mondays in particular. He simply objected to the rather rude manner in which they interrupted his perfectly good Sundays."
